{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' .mhl/specification/idea.accepted.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"constraints\":[\"Use .NET/C#, ASP.NET Core, Postgres, and Docker Compose with one local Postgres service and a persistent volume.\",\"Use Vertical Slice Architecture with a minimal shared kernel; do not introduce generic Controller, Service, or Repository layers.\",\"Use real Postgres for integration tests, with isolated and serial test execution; in-memory or mock-only persistence is not acceptable.\",\"Configure the connection through TODO_DB_CONNECTION with only a documented local default; do not expose credentials or internal failure details.\",\"The scope is greenfield, local development/test use only, with no frontend, users/authentication, cloud or production deployment, legacy/JSON migration, or regulated-data claim.\"],\"desiredOutcomes\":[\"Provide the six task-management operations with a stable JSON and Problem Details HTTP contract.\",\"Persist tasks in a local Postgres database, automatically initialize the schema, and preserve id, title, and status across API-only restarts.\",\"Provide idempotent local startup and a single verification flow covering pure unit tests and real HTTP/Postgres integration tests.\",\"Keep endpoint behavior cohesive through vertical slices while validating inputs and sanitizing dependency failures.\"],\"openQuestions\":[{\"blocking\":false,\"id\":\"OQ-1\",\"question\":\"Which supported .NET SDK, Postgres image, and exact library versions should be pinned for implementation?\"},{\"blocking\":false,\"id\":\"OQ-2\",\"question\":\"Which local platform and named owners or reviewers should be recorded when development begins?\"}],\"problem\":\"A local HTTP consumer needs a reliable way to create, query, filter, complete, edit, and remove tasks, with real Postgres persistence and reproducible verification instead of transient or legacy-file storage.\",\"schema\":\"iao/idea/v1\",\"title\":\"Local TodoApp WebAPI with persistent task management\",\"users\":[\"Unauthenticated local HTTP clients managing tasks\",\"Developers building and maintaining the API and local infrastructure\",\"Testers and reviewers verifying rules, endpoints, persistence, and failures\",\"The requester or designated acceptance reviewer\"]}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
